            <div xml:id="d5">

                <pb facs="0094" n="4" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg4"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/984: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-17T10:00:00+08:00">January 17, 1934—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 17—4:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>42. The following telegram has been received from the Consul General at Harbin:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“January 16, 11 a.m. Japanese Consul General confirms report that Pu Yi
                            will be made Emperor on March 1st.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
